        // In the README and UI:
        // 1. In Telegram, search for BotFather and start a chat.
        // 2. Send the command /newbot and follow BotFather's instructions to create a new bot.
        // 3. After creating the bot, BotFather will provide you with a bot token. Copy this token.
        // 4. In the bot's settings, set the 'Web App' parameter to your web app's URL (e.g., https://your-webapp-url.com).
        // 5. Start a chat with your bot, and it should open your web app inside Telegram.
      </element>
    </insert>
  </files>
</diff>
```

**Finalizing Type Declarations**

I'm now completing the type definitions for the Telegram Web App within my application. I need to make the type definition comprehensive. I'm focusing on ensuring everything is correctly typed to avoid runtime errors, especially concerning the `MainButton` attributes and methods. Specifically, I'm integrating Telegram Web App types within the existing `Window` interface to include features such as the `ready`, `expand`, `close`, `MainButton` which incorporates things like `text`, `color`, `textColor`, `isVisible`, `show`, `hide`, etc.

```xml
<diff>
  <files>
    <insert path="src/types.ts">
      <element type="typescript">
        declare global {
          interface Window {
            Telegram?: {
              WebApp: {
                ready: () => void;
                expand: () => void;
                close: () => void;
                MainButton: {
                  text: string;
                  color: string;
                  textColor: string;
                  isVisible: boolean;
                  show: () => void;
                  hide: () => void;
                  setText: (text: string) => void;
                  textColor: string;
                  color: string;
                  enable: () => void;
                  disable: () => void;
                  onClick: (callback: () => void) => void;
                  offClick: (callback: () => void) => void;
                };
                BackButton: {
                  show: () => void;
                  hide: () => void;
                  onClick: (callback: () => void) => void;
                  offClick: (callback: () => void) => void;
                };
                // Add more Telegram Web App properties and methods as needed
              };
              // Add more Telegram properties as needed
            };
          }
        }

        export {};
      </element>
    </insert>
  </files>
</diff>
```

I have completed the type definition update. I have made the necessary type additions and ensured they are properly integrated within the application. The updated types include the `MainButton` attributes and methods, as well as the `BackButton`. I am adding support for further Telegram properties as needed. I am focusing on making the telegram integration types complete.


**Refining Data Handling**

I'm now integrating more data, so I have fixed a small bug. I needed to properly handle the formatted text output used within the checkout button. The main button text was not rendering correctly when `formatCurrency` was used, so it has been properly formatted to match the existing user interface. I am now making sure that the data transfer to telegram is working properly.


**Enhancing Currency Display**

I'm now refining the checkout button text formatting within `Cart.tsx`. I was not accounting for currency formatting in the main button. So, I need to make the amount display the correctly formatted currency. I am making sure the telegram integration handles all the data properly.


